# TeamGM Conventions

## UI: Tailwind + Gluestack

- Prefer **NativeWind / Tailwind** (`className`) for layout, spacing, colors, and typography whenever it applies.
- Use **Gluestack UI** components for UI primitives (Text, Box, VStack, Button, etc.). Do not use React Native `Text`/`View`/`Pressable` for new UI unless the user explicitly asks otherwise.
- **Screens** use root `VStack` with `className="flex-1 bg-teamgm-app …"`. Use `Box` for surfaces/cards only, not full-screen layout.
- Copy or extend components from `TeamGM/src/components/ui/` per Gluestack v3 patterns.
- **Brand colors** are defined in `TeamGM/tailwind.config.js` (`teamgm.*`) and sourced from `src/constants/brand-colors.js` (re-exported in `colors.ts`). Use Tailwind classes: `bg-teamgm-app`, `bg-teamgm-tab-bar`, `bg-teamgm-surface`, `text-teamgm-text-primary`, `text-teamgm-text-muted`.
- User-facing strings live in `src/constants/copy.ts`.
- Use `@/` imports (`@` → `src/`). Assets use `@/assets/...`.
- Legacy `ThemedText` / `ThemedView` are deprecated; migrate to Gluestack `Text` / `Box` with `className`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
import { Text, View, Pressable } from 'react-native';
<Pressable style={{ padding: 16 }}><Text>Save</Text></Pressable>

// ✅ GOOD
import { Box, Button, ButtonText } from '@/components/ui/button';
<VStack className="flex-1 bg-teamgm-app px-4 py-2">
  <Button><ButtonText>{LABELS.save}</ButtonText></Button>
</VStack>
```

## Logic: Evaluate Outside Conditionals

Compute flags, derived values, and handlers **before** `return` or JSX branches. Avoid heavy logic inside `if`, ternaries, or inline JSX.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
{items.length > 0 && user?.isPremium ? <ScoresList items={items} /> : <EmptyState />}

// ✅ GOOD
const hasScores = items.length > 0;
const canViewScores = hasScores && user?.isPremium;
// ...
return canViewScores ? <ScoresList items={items} /> : <EmptyState />;
```

## Text: Use Constants

All user-facing copy shown in text components must be **named constants** (file-level or shared `constants/copy.ts`), not inline string literals in JSX.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<Text>Scores</Text>

// ✅ GOOD
const LABELS = { scoresTitle: 'Scores' } as const;
<Text>{LABELS.scoresTitle}</Text>
```

## Comments

Add a **single-line** `//` comment on the line **immediately above**:

- Every function (components, hooks, helpers)
- Blocks of evaluation logic (derived state, memoized inputs, non-trivial assignments before render)

Do not add noisy comments on obvious one-liners. Keep comments short and purposeful.

```tsx
// Builds tab bar height including safe area inset
const tabBarHeight = TAB_BAR_CONTENT_HEIGHT + bottomInset;

// Root tab navigator for the app shell
export default function TabLayout() {
```
